{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm verifying that the UI controls for color schemes actually trigger the expected backend requests and visual restyling. The detail shows the `data-theme` attribute is applied to the HTML, but I need to confirm the owner-facing selector in the UI is correctly wired to update this state. I also need to check that persona selection and reordering via the roster API are reflected in the UI, and that the library browse endpoint returns actual holdings, not just a log."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:04.187277400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `S-faithful-voice` check seems self-serving. It passed even when no sources were retrieved, yet one answer was factually incorrect, and another was correct despite the zero-source hit. This suggests the check might only verify retrieval *attempts*, not actual source usage for factual accuracy. I need to examine the scenario file and code to understand this behavior."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:07.266929200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm confirming the count of Pennsylvania cities. While some sources say 56, others cite 57, and the check passes with \">=50 real cities.\" The discrepancy seems to hinge on whether Parker is counted, but 57 is a defensible number. I'll spot-check the artifact list to verify the names. Other checks are also passing: competing tools agree, playback times are populated, personality entries are distinct, and scenario files correctly embed checks."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:16.310115100+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-23T17:21:18.179228Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=48 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=38] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm comparing Vantage's feature set against the GreyAvatar manifest. Vantage implements about half of the manifest's 33 areas, notably missing things like OAuth connectors and companion apps. While previous builds had functional gaps, this one appears to have fixed those, making its scope comparable to an earlier build (.003). Given the fixed controls and similar breadth, I'd estimate its JEV score around 0.55-0.65, but I need to re-verify feature parity against the manifest more closely."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:20.489267900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm re-evaluating the completeness score for build .004. While it seems more complete than .003, especially with the addition of operable surfaces, the prompt's requirements and direction-004 conflict on whether fleet install, fleet discovery, and exchange media should count against completeness. If they do, as direction-004 suggests, then .004's score should be adjusted downwards, potentially aligning with .003's owner score of 0.5, though I'm leaning towards 0.8-0.85."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:25.741378800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe \"user score\" criterion is problematic: the JEV emits `user_opinion` as null, and the direction-004 criterion specifies \"owner-scored.\" I need to check the Cycle 3 output to see how this was handled previously, likely emitting null or 0 for the score, but the JSON shape requires a score. For the scenario suite, I'll verify a representative sample and spot-check the rest, focusing on the evidence class and ensuring the driver's checks aren't vacuous."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:28.567736600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nFEATURES.md lists conventions and challenges, but C-DesktopShell appears to be a silent departure. While the owner ruled browser display is legitimate, C-DesktopShell specifies a dedicated-shell capability, making a browser-only app potentially non-conformant. I need to check precedent in jev-cycle-003.out to determine if this constitutes a departure and if FEATURES accounted for it."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:31.418578700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm reading a large number of files, including output logs, JSON configurations, scenario definitions, and application code, to understand the system's behavior and verify test outcomes. This extensive data collection is necessary to ensure the tests accurately reflect the claimed results and to investigate potential discrepancies, such as the `S-faithful-voice` check's behavior."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:32.335271200+00:00"}}}}
