{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe system correctly identified Harrisburg as the capital and appropriately flagged or withheld information for other queries. However, a persona-driven fabricated experience claim was made, which is distinct from factual hallucination. The accuracy of the Harrisburg response is borderline, as it was correct but lacked source grounding. The scoring mechanism appears self-serving by counting zero hits as a pass, and the live reply was not fidelity-checked. I need to examine the persona and grounding code to understand these discrepancies."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:51.196114600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"separated-salt","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to verify if the owner-facing selector is truly controlling the S-color-schemes. The current evidence shows a POST to a theme endpoint followed by an HTML response with `data-theme=\"dark\"`, but I'm unsure if the selector is the direct cause. I'll examine `scenarios.py`, `app.js`, and `styles.css` to trace the interaction from the selector to the API endpoint and the resulting theme rules."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:21:51.897495600+00:00"}}}}
